## arg 1:  the new package version
post_install() {
  cat <<'EOF'
t715-claude-code: the installer is in, not Claude Code itself (Anthropic's
licence). Nothing is preinstalled; the app drawer's "Claude Code installer"
opens a guided, opt-in install in a terminal (about 250 MB downloaded from
Anthropic, signature-verified against its release key).

    Claude Code installer      (drawer entry, or: t715-claude-guide)

which asks before doing anything, then runs the root wrapper itself:

    sudo t715-claude-install

After it succeeds, sign in as your user:

    claude setup-token
    claude-token-save     # paste the token at its prompt, not as an argument

See docs/DEPLOY.md 11.10.
EOF
}

## arg 1:  the new package version
## arg 2:  the old package version
post_upgrade() {
  post_install "$1"
}
